From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:26:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: asahi: enable transparent huge pages,
 madvise only

The page block cap says "THP is madvise only in our configs", but the
shared fragment never sets TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE and the packaged base
config has it off, so no Mac kernel built from them has THP at all: no
transparent_hugepage sysfs, no madvise(MADV_HUGEPAGE), no multi-size
THP, and no contiguous PTE mappings (ARM64_CONTPTE depends on it).

Measured on the J604 (M4, 16K pages): a random pointer chase over
512 MiB takes 107.0 ns per load on base pages and 97.8 ns on 32 MiB
hugetlb pages, the same walk, so TLB reach is worth 9 ns there.

Enable THP with madvise as the default, which is what the page block
cap was written for; nothing changes for memory that does not ask.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config b/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
index 8af592b1fb..60c4e09064 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/asahi.config
@@ -14,6 +14,9 @@ CONFIG_ARM64_MEMORY_MODEL_CONTROL=y
 # 16K pages make a page block 32 MiB, and khugepaged then sets min_free_kbytes
 # to 352 MiB on an 8 GB Mac. Keep page blocks at 2 MiB as on 4K kernels.
 CONFIG_PAGE_BLOCK_MAX_ORDER=7
+# THP for memory that asks for it (madvise), which the cap above assumes.
+CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE=y
+CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_MADVISE=y
 CONFIG_ARM_APPLE_CPUIDLE=y
 CONFIG_ARM_APPLE_SOC_CPUFREQ=m
 # The CLPC's power modes are platform profiles, and the platform_profile
-- 
